/// Public surface of the `text` device. Import `{ text }` and call `text.draw` / `text.clear`; the selected
/// backend (extras/text/<variant>) decides the sink. Both forward to the backend seams `text_be_draw` /
/// `text_be_clear`, so a driver's text code is identical across backends. Like `log`'s `msg`, the string is
/// `own` (moved into the FFI write) and its `.length` is read before the move to satisfy the extern-array
/// borrow rule; a `[]char` lowers to a bare pointer with the length passed explicitly.

/// Draw one run of text with its TOP-LEFT at render-pixel (x, y), `size`px tall, colour 0xRRGGBB.
draw :: func(x: int, y: int, own s: []char, size: int, color: int) -> Eff() {
  return text_be_draw(x, y, s, s.length, size, color);
}

/// Remove every previously drawn run (for a redraw / animated HUD).
clear :: func() -> Eff() {
  return text_be_clear();
}
